    "question": "There are 3 boxes of cereal. One box holds 14 ounces of cereal. Another box holds half the amount of the first box and 5 ounces less than the third box. How much cereal is there in all 3 cereal boxes?",
    "gold": "33",
    "answer": "First = <<14=14>>14 oz\nSecond = (1/2) * 14 = <<(1/2)*14=7>>7 oz\nThird = 7 + 5 = <<7+5=12>>12 oz\n14 + 7 + 12 = <<14+7+12=33>>33 oz\nThere are 33 ounces of cereal in those 3 boxes.\n#### 33"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total amount of cereal in all three boxes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the amount of cereal in the first box.\n2. Calculate the amount of cereal in the second box.\n3. Calculate the amount of cereal in the third box.\n4. Sum the amounts of cereal in all three boxes.\n\nLet's start with the first box. The first box holds 14 ounces of cereal.\n\nNext, we calculate the amount of cereal in the second box. The second box holds half the amount of the first box. Therefore, the amount of cereal in the second box is:\n\\[\n\\frac{14}{2} = 7 \\text{ ounces}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the amount of cereal in the third box. The third box holds 5 ounces more than the second box. Therefore, the amount of cereal in the third box is:\n\\[\n7 + 5 = 12 \\text{ ounces}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we sum the amounts of cereal in all three boxes:\n\\[\n14 + 7 + 12 = 33 \\text{ ounces}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total amount of cereal in all three boxes is \\boxed{33}.",
